/-
L4Factoidal.Crypto.RsaOaepTests — build-time `#guard`s for
`Crypto/RsaOaep.lean` (RSAES-OAEP, RFC 8017 §7.1;
https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/1082).

A `#guard` runs in the Lean interpreter, which cannot call an `@[extern]`,
so the RSA operations here are `refOp`: `y^x mod n` over Lean's `Nat`, a
TEST REFERENCE ONLY (the `SAML` tests use the same construction). It is
never used outside this file and it is not constant time. The padding under
test is the production one: `RsaOaep.oaepEncrypt`, `oaepDecrypt`,
`emeEncode`, `emeDecode`. The HACL* operations are checked at run time by
section `rsa-oaep` of `Harness/CryptoProbe.lean`.

Vectors (the hex below was generated by a script from the files, not typed
by hand):

  * RSA Laboratories `oaep-vect.txt`, Example 1 key (1024 bits), OAEP
    Example 1.1: SHA-1, MGF1-SHA-1, empty label, given seed. File:
    `third_party/testing/rsa-oaep-vect/oaep-vect.txt` (sha256
    abca68e5176027ac98af1a4100b73e06bf2b36054d3f13f6a10e2fe603e8af4f; see
    the PROVENANCE.md beside it).
  * Wycheproof `rsa_oaep_2048_sha1_mgf1sha1_test.json` tcId 6 (valid) and
    12 (InvalidOaepPadding), and `rsa_oaep_2048_sha256_mgf1sha256_test.json`
    tcId 6 and 9 (valid; 9 has a label) and 12, 13, 14
    (InvalidOaepPadding), from the `third_party/testing/wycheproof`
    submodule (C2SP/wycheproof, Apache-2.0).
-/
